invariant: INV-50
file: sha512.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: the second arm's finalize, the reference a device object runs,
  writes zero as the upper word of the length where FIPS 180-4 §5.1.2
  writes the upper 64 bits of the bit count. Every message under 2^61
  bytes has the same digest, so the published vectors pass, the first
  arm still agrees with this one in every case that hashes a message,
  and no proof holds a value. test/sha512_portable.c compiles this arm
  into bin/sha2_equiv_test, which starts a context at a byte count of
  2^61 - 1 and at larger ones on it and compares the digest with one
  whose padding the test writes from a 128-bit product
  (test/sha2_equiv_length512.h).

--- old
// (docs/proofs.md: keep harness-reachable loop structure concrete).
static void finalize(sha512 *s) {
    uint64_t high = s->total_bytes >> 61;
--- new
// (docs/proofs.md: keep harness-reachable loop structure concrete).
static void finalize(sha512 *s) {
    uint64_t high = 0;
